{:edb/db-before-t 849 :edb/db-after-t 850 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534162 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:21:27.061Z" 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186055075 1068 #edb/ref 17592186051933 13194139534162 17592186045417 false] [17592186055075 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412776 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186055075 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186055075 1071 "If $A = {1, 4, 7, …, 295}$, then $\\mid A|=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139534162 17592186045417 false] [17592186055075 1071 "If $A={1,4,7,…,295},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186055075 1074 "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,4,\\,7,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =7-4 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =1+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={3n-2:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3N-2 & =295 \\\\ 3N & =297 \\\\ N & =\\frac{297}{3} \\\\ N & =99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={3n-2:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 99}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $99$ elements, we must have $|A|=99.$" 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186087969 1068 #edb/ref 17592186084548 13194139534162 17592186045417 false] [17592186087969 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412775 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186087969 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186087969 1074 "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{y-1}={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation cannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $\\frac{1}{y-1}$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412777 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412778 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412779 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412780 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412781 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1043 #edb/ref 17592186412782 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045460 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1045 "Quiz 1" 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1046 #edb/ref 17592186412782 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412768 1053 #uuid "248e0d07-4285-57ca-807a-b5e68115c826" 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412769 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" 13194139534162 17592186045417 true] [17592186412769 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534162 1759